Building dosdumb.exe (DUMB for MS-DOS)
======================================

dosdumb.exe needs DJGPP 2.05 and Allegro 4.2.  There are two ways to
build it; both make DOSDUMB.EXE, DOOM4DUM.WAD and HTIC4DUM.WAD, and
add GAME.WAD, the DUMB game (https://github.com/cadwal/dumb-game,
branch modernize).

To run it, put these next to each other with CWSDPMI.EXE and start
it in DOS, DOSBox or DOSBox-X:

  DOSDUMB.EXE -w GAME.WAD     the DUMB game; needs nothing else
  DOSDUMB.EXE                 Doom data: needs DOOM.WAD (Doom's, or
                              Freedoom's freedoom1.wad) and DOOM4DUM.WAD

DUMB logs to stdout, so adding "> DUMB.LOG" avoids the screen jumping.

Linux (or macOS): cross-compiling
---------------------------------

  dos/cross-build.sh [--iwad FILE | --freedoom] [--run]

Downloads the build-djgpp cross toolchain and Allegro 4.2, builds
them, builds DUMB with configure --host=i586-pc-msdosdjgpp, clones
and builds the DUMB game (with netpbm; otherwise its prebuilt
game.wad is used), and puts the result in build-dos/dist with
CWSDPMI.EXE and a dosbox.conf.  The package plays the DUMB game;
with --iwad FILE or --freedoom it plays that Doom data instead.
--run starts it in DOSBox-X or DOSBox.
See the comment at the top of the script for options and requirements.

  dos/get-cwsdpmi.sh [DIR]

Only downloads CWSDPMI.EXE (from csdpmi7b.zip) into DIR.  If no
CWSDPMI mirror can be reached, it installs HDPMI32.EXE from the HX
DOS extender's GitHub releases instead (freeware).  HDPMI32 has to
be loaded before dosdumb.exe with "hdpmi32 -r"; the dosbox.conf
from cross-build.sh does that.

Windows: building inside DOSBox-X
---------------------------------

  dos\dosbox-x-build.cmd [-Iwad FILE | -Freedoom] [-GameWad FILE]
                         [-BuildOnly] [-Rebuild]

(or: powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File dos\dosbox-x-build.ps1)

Needs DOSBox-X (https://dosbox-x.com/).  Downloads DJGPP 2.05 (djdev,
gcc, binutils, make), CWSDPMI, Allegro 4.2 and the DUMB game's
prebuilt game.wad (game.wad can't be built in DOS: it needs netpbm);
sets them up with a copy of this tree on a DOS C: drive in
build-dosbox\c; then starts DOSBox-X, which builds Allegro and DUMB
with the native DOS tools and runs DOSDUMB.EXE -w GAME.WAD.  With
-Iwad FILE or -Freedoom it plays that Doom data instead.  Logs go to
build-dosbox\c\LOGS.  Compiling under emulated DOS is slow, especially
the first Allegro build.  Run "Get-Help dos\dosbox-x-build.ps1 -Full"
for all options.

Files
-----

  cross-build.sh       Linux/macOS cross build (uses configure)
  get-cwsdpmi.sh       download CWSDPMI
  dosbox-x-build.ps1   Windows: set up and run the DOSBox-X build
  dosbox-x-build.cmd   runs the .ps1 without changing execution policy
  makefile.dj          plain makefile for DJGPP make, without configure
  config.h, dircfg.h   the configure results for DJGPP, for makefile.dj

docs/dos/MODERNIZE.md has the background.
